{
  "_comment": [
    "SHARED FRAME-INTEGRITY ORACLE (change frame-integrity, D5 / task 4.2).",
    "Generated — do not hand-edit. Regenerate with:",
    "swift run --package-path openspec/changes/frame-integrity/oracle-gen FrameIntegrityOracleGen",
    "Two byte-identical copies are committed, one per test tree, and both suites assert every case",
    "and all three pinned fields (verdict, reject_reason, meta), so neither platform can move its",
    "verifier without the other's suite going red.",
    "verdict       = ParsedFrame.ok, the verifier's FULL verdict.",
    "reject_reason = the Swift FrameRejectReason rawValue; Kotlin maps its enum through wireName.",
    "meta          = classifyHistoricalMeta, as start | complete | other | end(unix=U,trim=T).",
    "ecg_inner_payload_hex is present only on cases with ecg_path true (the second verifying path,",
    "Whoop5Ecg.innerPayload); null means that path refused the frame.",
    "The export FORM of a reject reason differs by design (Kotlin omits the key when there is no",
    "reason, Swift always writes it) — this oracle pins the verdict, the reason and the",
    "classification, never the export spelling."
  ],
